<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese money supply growth slows in Oct.</title>
<headline>Portuguese money supply growth slows in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese money supply, as measured by &quot;aggregate 'L&quot;, roughly equivalent to M3, rose 7.9 percent year-on-year in October, compared with 8.3 percent in September, the Bank of Portugal said.</p>
<p> Percentage change	 Oct 1996	  Sept 1996</p>
<p> Aggregate 'L'		+7.9		 +8.3</p>
<p> Domestic bank lending    +8.1		 +6.9</p>
<p>Note - Plus sign denotes growth, a minus sign denotes a fall.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
